# Facet

## Overview

Facet is a match game of cut stones, played in the browser on a lit gem board.
The board is a square grid, every cell holding one gem. The player swaps two
neighboring gems, any line of three or more of one kind shatters, the stones
above fall into the gap, and fresh stones drop in from the top to fill it.

Facet's defining idea is strain. Every clear presses on the gems around it, and
a gem that has taken enough of that pressure is flawed. A flawed gem shatters
with any clear that touches it and is worth double, so a swap made beside a worn
stretch of the board runs on into a long chain.

Facet has its own name, look, and rules, and its assets, branding, and design
are original to it.

The specification spans several files under `specs/`. `specs/board.md` gives the
board, its cell geometry, the gem kinds and cuts, strain, and the notation
boards are written in; `specs/rules.md` the rules a swap is accepted under and
the rules a chain step resolves by, together with scoring, levels, and the end
of a round; `specs/controls.md` the pointer that plays the board and works every
screen, and the keys the menus answer; `specs/state.md`
what the game's state carries; `specs/instrumentation.md` the debug and
automation surface; `specs/ui.md` the screens, the menus, and the audio cues;
`specs/assets.md` the art, effects, and sounds the build produces and ships; and
`specs/showcase.md` the store-page presentation that ships beside the game. Read
all of them and build the game they describe as one cohesive whole.

Much of the game's look and all of its sound come from files produced during
this build. `specs/assets.md` states what is produced, with which tool, where
each file lands, and what stays drawn in code.

