## The runtime

The game is built on the {{engine.name}} engine, which documents itself in the
`engine/` directory at the root of this repository. It is a gameplay framework
as much as a runtime: the game is written as subclasses of its classes, a game
instance, a game mode, actors and their components, and the controllers that
drive them, and the engine constructs, ticks, and renders them in a fixed
order. It owns the frame loop and the delta time the game is given, rendering
and the camera, the canvas fit, the input actions the menus are driven by, the
pointer the board is played with, audio cues, asset loading, and the debug
overlay. Read its documentation before you start. This specification
states only what is specific to Facet.

The logical design field handed to the engine is the stage, and the game leaves
the camera at rest, so world units and the stage's logical units coincide and
every position in this specification is both. The pointer reaches the game from
the engine already in those units, as ordered samples carrying its press and
release edges. `specs/controls.md` states what Facet does with them.
{{/if}}

## The project you build in

The project at the root of this repository is already wired up, and its
`README.md` describes it. It is a TypeScript project built with Vite, tested
with Vitest, linted with ESLint, and formatted with Prettier. That toolchain is
fixed and supplied.

